<title>USA: FSA qualifies 21 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 21 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said on Tuesday that it qualified for bond insurance the following 21 issues scheduled for competitive sale:</p>
<p>--Jefferson County Board Of Ed, Ala., $9.045 million capital outlay bonds.</p>
<p>--North Mahaska Central School District, Iowa, $4.04 million General Obligation (GO) bonds.</p>
<p>--Junction City, Kan., $3.04 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Crowley, La., Imp series B, $4.04 million.</p>
<p>--Crowley, La., Imp series A, $4.83 million.</p>
<p>--Southbridge, Mass., $3.375 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Breitung Township School District, Mich., $3.75 million.</p>
<p>--Monroe County, Mich., $2.595 million water supply system.</p>
<p>--Andover, Minn., $3.12 million GO improvement.</p>
<p>--Battle Lake ISD #542, Minn., $7.9 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Polk County, Minn., $1.39 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Gaston County, N.C., $31.35 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Toms River Board of Education, N.J., $21.6 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Clark County, Nev., $70 million highway bonds.</p>
<p>--Burnt Hills-Ballston, N.Y. $2.079 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cambridge Central School Districts, N.Y. $2.25 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Whitney Point Central School District, N.Y., $3.689 million.</p>
<p>--Denton, Texas, $4.7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Germantown, Wis., $2.535 million GOs.</p>
<p>--West Allis, Wisc., $1.205 million GOs tax.</p>
<p>--West Allis, Wisc., $2.845 million GOs promissary.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
